or | Age 60 | Compensation: $2.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $1.2M ranks in the below the sector median among Energy peers, with revenue falling 21%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $285K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $11K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Excelerate Energy, Inc. is a mid-cap energy business with a $3.8B market cap on $1.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -21% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome. Operating margins are expanding by +4.7pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 63% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 54-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $298M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 24 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 11.77\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 3.3\u00d7.","Net dilution runs at 5.1% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 2.0\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 105% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.053267494376679},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Energy peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (13.0% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Energy tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Energy peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Energy sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 8% over 3 months"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Excelerate Energy (NYSE:EE) Draws Strong Rating Support. What\u2019s Next?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/energy/excelerate-energy-nyseee-draws-strong-rating-support-whats-next","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795182720.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.939,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"BMO Real Financial Progress Index: Latinos en EE. UU. recortan sus gastos festivos por casi $1,000 en medio de la doble celebracin festiva","sou